sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS 1 (tokens minted at admission, vault; no private-material callback) and R2-R3. docs/reference/tasks.md#dependency-batch-squash-admission.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · Services API (tasks-dependency-merge)
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as Services Node<br/>dependency batches
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>repository · PRs
  CLI->>GW: Merge batch of group 42<br/>publish #5165 · head 9f3c…
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `POST /api/v1/task-groups/42/dependency-merge` with `publish_operation_id` 5165, `head_sha` and an `Idempotency-Key`
  %%> - syntax: the MCP tool `tasks-dependency-merge` with `group`, `publish_operation_id`, `head_sha`
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - only the configured Services Node; there is no `orbit` command
  Note over GW: Check the batch<br/>task #5166 · mint 2 tokens
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the Project has dependency merge enabled; today every Project is off
  %%> - the Project is an app with a hosted production Instance; packages and unclassified monorepos are refused
  %%> - group 42 is an external dependency batch the Services Node created, with a passed handoff check and the exact successful publish task #5165 for this head
  %%> - no other task runs on group 42; the Gateway holds one lock per group
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - mints a write token with only `contents: write` and `pull_requests: write`, never `workflows: write`
  %%> - mints a read token with `contents`, `checks` and `actions` read
  %%> - pushes both to the vault as `dependency-merge-5166-write` and `-read` after commit (R3); no step fetches them from the Gateway
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5166 recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-dependency-merge
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209); no Node is a target
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the repository, default branch, PR branch `task-42`, expected head, and the smoke workflow path
  %%> - the vault key names of the tokens, never the tokens
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5166
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the caller follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>GH: Read the PR and checks<br/>Required checks · smoke
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the PR fresh, with the read token from `vault.get`
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - a PR that is not open, is a draft, comes from another repository, or targets another branch
  %%> - `Required checks` or `Production smoke / smoke` missing, pending, skipped or failed on the exact head
  SW->>GH: Read the changed files<br/>paged PR files · manifests
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads every changed file; only root `composer.json`, `composer.lock`, `package.json` and the npm, pnpm and Bun text lock files may change; Yarn and `bun.lockb` go the ordinary PR path
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - incomplete or capped file evidence, or any other file
  Note over SW: Check the dependency diff<br/>versions only · lock sources
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - compares base and head manifests: only versions of existing dependencies may differ
  %%> - checks every locked package against Packagist or the npm registry, and that it is reachable from the root manifest
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - a breaking semver bump: `dependency_merge.major_bump`; the PR stays open for hand-testing
  SW->>GH: Squash on expected head<br/>PUT pulls/57/merge · sha
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - squash-merges PR #57 only if its head still equals the expected head, with the write token
  %%> Lost reply:
  %%> - the next attempt reads PR #57 first; a merged exact head returns its merge SHA without another write
  SW->>GH: Revoke the tokens<br/>DELETE /installation/token
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - revokes both tokens, on success and on failure
  %%> If it fails:
  %%> - the run still reports its result; the tokens expire within one hour
  alt merged
    GH-->>SW: PR #57 merged · sha
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the merge commit
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · merge sha
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the merge<br/>task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5166 succeeds with the merge SHA
    %%> - the task system sees the merge and completes group 42 as usual; nothing is deployed here
  else refused or failed
    GH--xSW: check or diff refused
    %%> When:
    %%> - a check, file or diff rule refuses, the head moved, or GitHub refuses the merge
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Mark the task failed<br/>PR open · normal PR path
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5166 fails; PR #57 stays open and goes through ordinary PR handling
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - a new request for the same head is a new task with new tokens; it reads everything again
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5166
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
